  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) was very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal. With only two data points, the key uncertainty is whether the profile structure (single vs. multi) adds meaningful information beyond what a single profile captures. Question tested: config_002 isolates the multiprofile + avgpool aggregation effect while holding the RNA encoder (pca_n2000) constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison to config_001. Why best next: It is the most controlled experiment available—changing only profile_setting and adding aggregation—so any performance delta can be attributed to multiprofile structure. The result will determine whether to invest subsequent experiments in multiprofile variants (including multimodal) or to focus on encoder improvements, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a tight budget."
}

